                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="wcm/foundation/components/text"
                    text="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;>&lt;b>ADMINISTRATIVE REVIEW OF EMPLOYEE PERFORMANCE&lt;br>&#xa;Complete this form if you have been notified that you have been selected as an Administrative Reviewer.&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                    textIsRich="true">
                    <cq:responsive jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured">
                        <default
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            offset="1"
                            width="10"/>
                    </cq:responsive>
                </text>
                <text_452382839
                    jcr:created="{Date}2020-02-10T23:16:56.219-08:00"
                    jcr:createdBy="admin"
                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2020-02-11T01:21:10.125-08:00"
                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="foundation/components/text"
                    text="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;>&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;u>&lt;b>Introduction&lt;/b>&lt;/u>&lt;br>&#xa;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>The Administrative Review process provides selected individuals with an opportunity to offer feedback on the performance of a particular management&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; employee.&lt;br>&#xa;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>If you feel that your interactions with the indicated employee during the current review period have been too infrequent or too superficial to allow you&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; to provide an informed assessment of his or her performance, enter your name in the space for &amp;quot;Name of Evaluator&amp;quot; and check the box under &amp;quot;Basis for&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Evaluation.&amp;quot; &amp;nbsp;Do not complete the remainder of the form, but return the document to the indicated supervisor.&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                    textIsRich="true">
                    <cq:responsive jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured">
                        <default
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            offset="1"
                            width="10"/>
                    </cq:responsive>
                </text_452382839>
                <text_869179227
                    jcr:created="{Date}2020-02-10T23:18:06.056-08:00"
                    jcr:createdBy="admin"
                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2020-02-10T23:18:19.110-08:00"
                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="foundation/components/text"
                    text="&lt;p>&lt;u>&lt;b>Instructions&lt;/b>&lt;/u>&lt;br>&#xa;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>BASIS FOR EVALUATION&lt;/b>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>1. Explain how you have come to have knowledge of the employee's performance and how extensive your interactions are. &amp;nbsp;(Be as specific as possible.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>2.&amp;nbsp;How frequently do you interact with the employee? (e.g., daily? &amp;nbsp;weekly? &amp;nbsp;monthly?)&lt;br>&#xa;For what purposes do you interact with the employee? &amp;nbsp;(e.g., to develop policy, to do &amp;nbsp; committee work, to obtain information about . . . , to coordinate processes and procedures, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                    textIsRich="true"/>
                <text_1234943307
                    jcr:created="{Date}2020-02-10T23:18:24.506-08:00"
                    jcr:createdBy="admin"
                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2020-02-10T23:18:38.704-08:00"
                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="foundation/components/text"
                    text="&lt;p>&lt;b>PERFORMANCE ASSESSMENT&lt;/b>&lt;br>&#xa;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>1. On the basis of your firsthand knowledge, give specific examples of situations in which the employee has functioned effectively as a manager. &amp;nbsp;Your assessment will carry more weight if it is detailed and specific rather than broad and categorical. &amp;nbsp;Content is more important than quantity; a few concrete examples of effective performance are more useful than generalizations drawn from your observation of this employee. &amp;nbsp;In short, you should seek to provide information upon which the supervisors can base conclusions about the employee's performance.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>2. On the basis of your firsthand knowledge, describe specific areas in which you believe the employee's performance could be strengthened. &amp;nbsp;Again, strive to present the facts upon which your conclusions are based rather than your conclusions alone. &amp;nbsp;Be specific, and, if possible, offer suggestions as to how employee's performance could be improved.&lt;br>&#xa;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>&lt;b>ANONYMITY&lt;/b>&lt;br>&#xa;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>You can provide information anonymously by choosing not to sign the form. &amp;nbsp;Administrative Review forms must be shared with the MPP employee if so requested.&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                    textIsRich="true"/>
            </responsivegrid_436751876>
